        "title": "Render bridge-owned adjacency as openings in workspace graph borders",
        "body": "Goal: Render bridge-owned adjacency as openings in workspace graph borders\nStatus: in-progress\n\nTasks in scope:\n1. Resolve bridge adjacency from authored refs\n2. Compute stable frame aperture geometry\n3. Render graph borders with bridge openings\n4. Render bridge role and adjacency cues\n\nOpen questions:\n1. Should one bridge open both facing graph borders?\n2. How should several bridges share one boundary?\n3. What should an aperture show when its target graph is closed?",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "startedAt": "",
        "completedAt": "",
        "externalRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/tasks/workspace-bridge-apertures/root.node",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "An authored bridge whose ref matches an open graph produces a stable, visible aperture between the graph frames.",
          "Removing the bridge removes the aperture; portals and provisional interGraph edges never create one.",
          "Moving or resizing either graph recomputes the aperture without changing either graph document or dirty state.",
          "Import/export role, grants, exposure, consumption, and graph-local edge behavior remain intact.",
          "The workspace minimap can consume the same derived adjacency without reconstructing bridge semantics."
        ]
      }
