        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Workspace Bridge Apertures\n\nRender an authored bridge as visible adjacency between graph frames. A bridge remains a real, graph-local node whose `data.bridge.ref` identifies another graph or resource. The workspace derives border openings from that node when the addressed graph is open.\n\n## Model boundary\n\n- Only authored `bridge` nodes authorize apertures.\n- Bridge node IDs remain local to their owning graph.\n- Import/export roles, grants, exposure, and selected surfaces keep their existing meaning.\n- Ordinary edges remain graph-local.\n- Portals and provisional `interGraph` edge references do not create bridge apertures.\n- Aperture geometry is workspace presentation and never dirties a graph document.\n\n## Rendering direction\n\n1. Resolve bridge refs against open workspace graph addresses.\n2. Derive facing boundary points from the bridge node and target graph frame.\n3. Render frame borders as segments with a visible opening at each resolved crossing.\n4. Preserve role and direction cues without inventing a target-side bridge node.\n5. Recompute geometry when frames move, resize, open, or close.\n\n## Delivery order\n\nStart with deterministic adjacency resolution and pure geometry. Then replace the solid frame stroke, add role-aware visual treatment and closed-target behavior, reuse the projection in the workspace minimap, and finish with model and browser smoke validation."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-bridge-apertures-declaration"
        }
      }
    },
