    {
      "id": "workspace-bridge-apertures-acceptance-contract",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Bridge Aperture Acceptance Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 1160,
        "y": -360
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 500,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Bridge Aperture Acceptance Contract\n\n## Model integrity\n\n- Every aperture traces to one authored `bridge` node in its owning graph.\n- A bridge addresses another graph/resource through its canonical ref; no shared bridge node ID is created.\n- Import/export role, grants, exposure, and selected surface remain authoritative.\n- Portals and provisional direct intergraph edges do not authorize apertures.\n- Ordinary edges remain graph-local.\n\n## Rendering integrity\n\n- Resolved bridge adjacency creates an unmistakable break or receiving treatment in the relevant graph borders.\n- Moving, resizing, activating, opening, or closing graph frames recomputes presentation without mutating graph content.\n- Multiple apertures avoid headers, rounded corners, and one another.\n- Invalid or unresolved bridges remain visibly diagnosable.\n\n## Delivery integrity\n\n- The main workspace and workspace minimap consume one derived adjacency model.\n- The initial implementation can ship before final minimap scope switching.\n- Focused unit tests, graph-signature checks, production build, and browser smoke validation pass."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-bridge-apertures-declaration"
        },
        "markdown": "# Bridge Aperture Acceptance Contract\n\n## Model integrity\n\n- Every aperture traces to one authored `bridge` node in its owning graph.\n- A bridge addresses another graph/resource through its canonical ref; no shared bridge node ID is created.\n- Import/export role, grants, exposure, and selected surface remain authoritative.\n- Portals and provisional direct intergraph edges do not authorize apertures.\n- Ordinary edges remain graph-local.\n\n## Rendering integrity\n\n- Resolved bridge adjacency creates an unmistakable break or receiving treatment in the relevant graph borders.\n- Moving, resizing, activating, opening, or closing graph frames recomputes presentation without mutating graph content.\n- Multiple apertures avoid headers, rounded corners, and one another.\n- Invalid or unresolved bridges remain visibly diagnosable.\n\n## Delivery integrity\n\n- The main workspace and workspace minimap consume one derived adjacency model.\n- The initial implementation can ship before final minimap scope switching.\n- Focused unit tests, graph-signature checks, production build, and browser smoke validation pass."
      }
    }
